WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.600
Hello everybody. My name is Markiplier,

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.640
and welcome to Emporium.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.060
Now I wanted to warn you guys

00:00:05.140 --> 00:00:06.860
before we get into this;

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:08.700
this game apparently covers themes of

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.120
suicide, and maybe even darker subjects.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:13.460
So, I just wanted to warn you guys

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:14.620
before getting into it, because

00:00:14.620 --> 00:00:16.760
this will probably get dark,

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.080
and it will probably get sad.

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:21.240
So, I don't what to expect about it,

00:00:21.240 --> 00:00:23.720
because, apparently, it's some sort of artistic

00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:24.440
look at it-

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.560
"Analogies for personhood, for the self,

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:29.140
for consciousness, exert great power on our thinking,

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:31.580
and to think of consciousness as a locked chamber,

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:34.440
to think of the contents of that chamber as perception

00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:39.140
that will thus seem *ilu-e- ineloostibly private,

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:42.180
to think of our experiencing of the world as hidden,

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:44.260
but hidden inwardly."

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:45.960
*ineluctably?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.860
ineluctably private.

00:00:47.860 --> 00:00:49.180
I have never heard of that word.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:51.440
I have a pretty extensive vocabulary,

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.860
but I have never heard of

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:54.460
ineluctably.

00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.480
*unexpected thump*

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:58.040
Ah. Okay, thumpy thump win for me, huh?

00:00:58.600 --> 00:00:59.100
Oh.

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:02.240
Ah.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.020
Hi?

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:10.840
Uh?

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:12.040
*another unexpected thump*

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:12.760
O-Oh.

00:01:16.280 --> 00:01:16.780
Ohh.

00:01:19.940 --> 00:01:20.740
Oh.

00:01:22.540 --> 00:01:23.160
Okay.

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:30.580
Oh.

00:01:34.420 --> 00:01:36.500
OK. Oh, I'm moving.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.120
Alrighty then. Welp yep.

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:39.920
Wander right into Emporium.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.540
This seems like a good idea.

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:42.820
OK.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.660
I don't know why I'm going in here, but alright.
*thumping becomes more intense*

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:48.520
Did I just fall from the roof?

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.620
Why was I lying- bloody- in the middle of the Rooa-

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.740
-OK hi.

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:55.000
What the Hell is this?

00:01:56.740 --> 00:01:57.720
My God.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.420
This is so crazy.

00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:04.140
Look at this place- Oh hi there!

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:06.300
Can you help me understand what the Hell is going on here,

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.540
because I seem to be missing something here.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:11.240
Hey, buddy. How's it going? How are you doing?

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.700
The boy did nothing, just looked up at me.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.300
There was a flicker of recognition,

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:24.360
and I felt like a time traveler.

00:02:25.420 --> 00:02:28.880
He seemed unsure of what to say next."

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.040
I met my father only once, or my mother raised me poorly?!

00:02:36.740 --> 00:02:38.960
Aahh! I don't know!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:41.300
I don't know!

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.940
Is this important?! I don't know!

00:02:46.780 --> 00:02:48.620
I met my father only once!

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:55.200
He spoke rapidly now, fantasy stories of super hero dads.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:02:57.720
*fwooooooooooosh*

00:02:57.740 --> 00:02:59.160
I don't think that's what I meant.

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.620
I knew them to be mostly untrue.

00:03:02.700 --> 00:03:05.720
But choose- chose to believe, regardless.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.020
OK.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:10.680
I don't know if I want to go in that trailer, sir.

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:14.920
I don't know if that's- alright. You know what I'm going to go in anyway.

00:03:15.660 --> 00:03:16.540
Oh my Gahd.

00:03:17.360 --> 00:03:19.180
This game is so-o weird,

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:20.820
and I love it.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:22.260
Like I LOVE it.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:24.560
It's weird, but it's cool.

00:03:25.020 --> 00:03:26.780
I am shipwrecked this morning.

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.380
Folded over into sorry waves.

00:03:30.960 --> 00:03:32.560
Water, water, everywhere.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:34.080
Oh.

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:36.380
Why am I here?! What?!

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:39.700
The RV was just a piece of cardboard.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.400
Ohh, OK.

00:03:43.520 --> 00:03:47.920
I'm folded out onto the waves of the ocean! Where suddenly we're playing Raft again.

00:03:48.660 --> 00:03:51.820
Oh. Do I need to declare my loneliness to the world?

00:03:52.300 --> 00:03:53.280
Oh, boy.

00:03:54.220 --> 00:03:55.280
Oh, boy.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.820
Oh boy.

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:01.300
Oh, bo- oh, hi. There you are.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.360
I didn't even see you there.

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:07.320
I found myself busy. It whispers with some kind of ocean.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.560
I didn't notice the boy by my side, staring out, counting the waves.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:21.500
In a rushed fluster, the boy tugged my sleeve, and beckoned my ear closer.

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:22.700
*ghastly exhale*

00:04:25.980 --> 00:04:31.620
A child is only a child once, or I'd like to try and drown.

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.820
Ahhh. I wouldn't like to try that.

00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:38.060
That's like one of my worse ways I could possibly die.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:41.620
I'll go with, a child is only a child once, thank you.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:44.760
The boy spoke of a newly hatched egg.

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:46.340
Did I?!

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.700
The babe featherless. Breathless and still.

00:04:50.380 --> 00:04:52.520
Lost in some rotten tumble.

00:04:54.660 --> 00:04:55.900
Whoa.

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.840
The guy that made the visuals on this are really really cool.

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:02.300
Ah.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.080
I don't know what else you want from me.

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:08.000
Okay.

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:09.880
I guess I'll.. go back?

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:11.860
Can I go back now?

00:05:12.440 --> 00:05:14.020
La da dee doo doo doo-

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.460
Ooooooooooooo

00:05:17.520 --> 00:05:18.020
Kay.

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:18.920
That's a..

00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:19.960
That's a big building! (x1)

00:05:20.420 --> 00:05:21.920
That's a big building! (x2)

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:23.340
That's a big building! (x3)

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:24.440
That is a big building! (x4)

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.960
Eh, it popped up out of nowhere!

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:27.920
It's a big building!

00:05:29.880 --> 00:05:30.860
O-Oh... Hi.

00:05:31.440 --> 00:05:33.120
Okay, climby climb we go!

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.700
I don't know why we're here and I don't know who put it here.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:37.360
Ooh..

00:05:38.140 --> 00:05:39.380
It's uncomfortable..

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:39.900
Oh, hi.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:41.280
Okay, hello.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:43.100
Someone in there?

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:44.940
Why would someone be in there?

00:05:47.760 --> 00:05:48.260
Oh, hi.

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:50.540
Oh... Don't look at me like that.

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:51.920
Oh, don't do that to me.

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.180
Ohh-Don't look at me like that.!

00:05:56.480 --> 00:06:00.400
I was left in the company of my father for a single day.

00:06:03.060 --> 00:06:05.140
I don't believe he spoke at all.

00:06:05.740 --> 00:06:11.580
He just walked along that peer and held my hand while I toddled in tow.

00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:18.620
The impossible depth of that green grey water is all I remember clearly.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:23.280
So that has to do with the choice I made in the beginning of the game.

00:06:23.560 --> 00:06:24.120
I think.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.340
I'm pretty sure that would've changed.

00:06:26.440 --> 00:06:29.520
I don't know if this has multiple endings to this, I have no idea.

00:06:29.520 --> 00:06:31.520
I don't know the ramifications of these decisions.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.420
But, I'm sooooo curious.

00:06:36.620 --> 00:06:42.140
And also not curious because i'm not sure I wanna know where this is leading me to.

00:06:42.800 --> 00:06:46.220
Higher and higher I go in this tower in the middle of nowhere.

00:06:46.740 --> 00:06:48.820
Through halls that I can't control.

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:53.200
Oh.. Ah, Okay I'm back here but now there's a bird house!

00:06:53.520 --> 00:06:55.360
I think I understand the analogy of that!

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:57.860
FLY FREE pretty little birdy!

00:06:58.240 --> 00:06:59.180
Oh boy.

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:04.820
Wait, are we just starting over again?

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:07.640
Do I have to make all the choices?

00:07:08.260 --> 00:07:10.320
Do I have to make the *right* choices here?

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:11.380
I don't know!!

00:07:11.760 --> 00:07:12.640
I'm not sure!

00:07:12.920 --> 00:07:14.660
What's with the bird house?!

00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:17.500
Ookkaayy.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.940
Why is there an emporium?

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:21.140
Hello birdy birdy.

00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.020
The nesting box was no longer a home.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:30.420
I placed it here so the boy could listen for himself.

00:07:31.840 --> 00:07:34.900
That never ending, inconsolable cry.

00:07:34.900 --> 00:07:41.460
Emanating from such a tiny hole, powered by impossible acoustics.

00:07:42.480 --> 00:07:47.600
Okay, alright, good reminder! Thank you for that, I think.

00:07:47.860 --> 00:07:48.580
Thank you.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:50.060
Thank you for that.

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:53.400
If we go in here and I have to make different choices I'll do that but I do-

00:07:53.580 --> 00:07:54.080
Ookay.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:55.740
Ah.

00:07:55.900 --> 00:07:56.940
This is different.

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:00.460
That wasn't a trolley car there and there was no kitchen over there.

00:08:00.700 --> 00:08:02.000
I have no idea what this is..

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:03.140
Was I supposed to be looking at-

00:08:03.140 --> 00:08:03.640
Oh

00:08:04.180 --> 00:08:04.680
Hi.

00:08:05.260 --> 00:08:06.860
Ohhhhhh.

00:08:07.780 --> 00:08:10.800
The plaque read "Hiding place No. 08,"

00:08:11.540 --> 00:08:13.260
Or "Dinner with Mother."

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:14.840
Ohh.

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:17.160
Oh.

00:08:19.100 --> 00:08:20.340
That's sad..

00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:24.120
I didn't know that these were exhibits that I was supposed to look at.

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:28.500
The plaque read "Hiding place No. 143,"

00:08:28.940 --> 00:08:29.440
Or,

00:08:29.540 --> 00:08:30.580
"Stationary."

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:33.360
Hundred forty-three?!

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.580
How many hiding places do you need?!

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.940
Why do you need so many hiding spaces?

00:08:39.400 --> 00:08:40.280
What is happening?

00:08:42.240 --> 00:08:46.020
The plaque read "Hiding place No. 00,"

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:51.060
Eugh, alrighty then. Well I can't go-

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:52.000
Ooo

00:08:52.360 --> 00:08:53.040
Kay.

00:08:53.080 --> 00:08:56.180
Alright, oh the camera is going fuckey on me.

00:08:56.220 --> 00:08:58.780
The plaque read "Hiding place No. 06,"

00:08:59.360 --> 00:08:59.860
Or,

00:09:00.360 --> 00:09:01.420
"Wooden Masks"

00:09:01.960 --> 00:09:02.920
Fascinating.

00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:07.260
Okay, so I'm going to talk to the guy but this is definitely different right?

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:08.780
I'm not crazy here.

00:09:09.140 --> 00:09:10.260
It's different.

00:09:10.420 --> 00:09:10.980
I think.

00:09:11.440 --> 00:09:12.320
I don't know.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.060
I tried to remember what it was like to be young.

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:20.980
Perhaps the boy would remind me.

00:09:21.560 --> 00:09:23.560
Perhaps it would make a difference.

00:09:25.520 --> 00:09:26.020
Oh.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:28.780
I can think myself invisible.

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.940
Being alone is part of survival.

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:39.220
I kinda disagree with one of those, but I don't think I can think myself invisible

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:41.840
But that like, relates to all the hiding places, I guess.

00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:43.640
Kind of? In a way?

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:48.960
The boy's voice deepened now. He spoke slow, low, and quiet.

00:09:49.640 --> 00:09:54.260
His words came from me as if from inside my own chest.

00:09:55.300 --> 00:10:00.020
And as they did, I swear I saw him blur around the edges.

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:05.640
Okay. That's weird. Yeah, okay, I'll step into your weird RV home.

00:10:05.900 --> 00:10:09.060
I'm sure nothing horrible is gonna happen.

00:10:11.060 --> 00:10:14.860
Am I gonna awaken on a pier again or am I gonna go somewhere else?

00:10:16.380 --> 00:10:18.300
I had a heady notion to flee.

00:10:19.460 --> 00:10:24.000
The sensation had come fast, and I found it intoxicating.

00:10:25.040 --> 00:10:26.320
I needed to vanish.

00:10:27.220 --> 00:10:31.680
And have the void left in my wake shrink up behind me.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.940
Oh, this is different.

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:36.060
Oh.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:38.280
Ah.

00:10:39.580 --> 00:10:42.080
Okay. Well, there's the trolley car.

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:45.280
What is all of this?

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:51.260
Oh, man. It's so weird. I've never really seen a game told from this perspective before.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:59.400
Just let alone the isometric view of it, but like, from such a distant shot, too. Like it's really, really cool.

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:02.160
Oops, almost missed my target there. Dur-di-durski!

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.980
Oh man, what the hell happened over there?

00:11:05.360 --> 00:11:07.280
I mean, I know none of this is actual reality here, but...

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:08.940
Oh, boy.

00:11:10.160 --> 00:11:15.340
"I once lent on this bridge, ready to take myself over its barrier.

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:23.460
"Hoping for one of the ancient locomotives to rattle forth and run me through." Ugh!

00:11:24.140 --> 00:11:30.140
"I waited a lifetime before I realized  all the trains had stopped running.

00:11:31.800 --> 00:11:35.140
"It was in this waiting that I first met the boy."

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:37.020
Oh.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:42.920
"Anything can crumble in an instant," or "To be still is to be peaceful."

00:11:47.400 --> 00:11:49.780
That sounds moderately pleasant.

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:52.100
I guess.

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:57.040
But also I kinda believe this one. Anything *can* crumble in an instant.

00:11:57.960 --> 00:12:01.040
I don't know! I'll go with the peaceful one!

00:12:02.140 --> 00:12:06.740
"The boy regaled me with our travels and commutes.

00:12:07.400 --> 00:12:10.600
"That kinetic score of steam and metal...

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.460
"How we wished for silence.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.000
"To be grave and static."

00:12:17.440 --> 00:12:21.580
Oh wait, unless you meant, like, to be still is- okay, that's all right then.

00:12:24.360 --> 00:12:28.340
Alrighty then. I'll be on my way. Unless you meant to be still is to be peaceful, as in...

00:12:30.140 --> 00:12:30.700
...death.

00:12:31.600 --> 00:12:35.680
'Cause that's not as nice as I might have thought that it would be.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:42.460
Anything can crumble in an instant, just the same as any trains can just fly off into  the sky.

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:45.060
And then be lost to the void!

00:12:47.620 --> 00:12:48.960
I have no idea what's happening.

00:12:50.000 --> 00:12:56.700
Okay, further up we go, I guess! Unless this is the exact same way to go, and then, honestly, who knows.

00:12:57.760 --> 00:12:58.260
Jeez.

00:12:59.660 --> 00:13:01.660
Hello. Hi.

00:13:02.340 --> 00:13:05.420
Do you have some mysteries to unfold for me?

00:13:08.420 --> 00:13:11.160
Oh, don't look at me like that. I still don't like it.

00:13:12.060 --> 00:13:14.060
Just compared to the last one, I don't think I'll like it.

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.980
"I have a superpower that no one else knows about.

00:13:21.340 --> 00:13:26.400
"I discovered this when I was 6 years old." Is it to be invisible?

00:13:26.920 --> 00:13:31.580
"I would let my breathing shallow and keep myself perfectly still.

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:36.840
"Before I knew it, I would fade into something almost like water.

00:13:37.580 --> 00:13:41.540
"And seep through every crack in the earth."

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:47.320
I don't know what that means, and I don't know how useful that superpower is. That seems...

00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:52.180
Seems weird, and uh... metaphorical, even.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.500
Oh! We're still going up!

00:13:56.840 --> 00:13:58.840
We didn't get sent out into the abyss!

00:13:59.780 --> 00:14:02.720
Okay. Unless I didn't get sent out into the abyss before. I don't remember.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:04.020
I can't remember!

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:08.480
Are we going back? Are we gonna go back? Do we have to go back?

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:10.320
I don't know!

00:14:11.740 --> 00:14:14.200
I don't know any- Oh, we're back now.

00:14:15.080 --> 00:14:19.340
Oh, good! Ah, yes, we have a new exhibit.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:23.480
Is there gonna be something poetic about that one, too?

00:14:23.660 --> 00:14:32.060
God, it seems like if I had to guess what's going on here, this guy is looping through his life after he...

00:14:32.420 --> 00:14:36.100
...threw himself from the roof of this building.

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:42.060
Whatever this building is. Like that splotch of blood on the ground is where he landed.

00:14:42.620 --> 00:14:44.620
"I had built a shrine to monotony.

00:14:45.300 --> 00:14:48.780
"There is a calm to be found in repetition." Heh!

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:55.140
"So I would busy myself in dizzy little circles until sick from the spin."

00:14:56.840 --> 00:15:03.640
Great. Is that like an easter egg? Am I supposed to dizzy myself in sweet circles until I'm sick from the spin?

00:15:03.640 --> 00:15:07.540
Because I can do that. (laughing) Here I go!

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:11.120
(uncomfortable laughing) Whee-hee-hee-hee! Whoo-hoo!

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:14.140
Aah, fun!

